#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:81
msgid "Flocculator to Floc Filter Transition"
msgstr "Floculador a transición filtro de flóculos "

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:83
msgid ""
"We now have a published AguaClara hydraulic flocculator model and we have "
"strong evidence that primary particles are removed first order with respect "
"to depth (or time) in the floc filter. Given these two models it is possible"
" for the first time to optimize the design of a flocculator based on "
"minimizing the volume of the flocculator and floc filter reactors."
msgstr ""
"Ahora disponemos de un modelo publicado de floculador hidráulico AguaClara y"
" tenemos pruebas sólidas de que las partículas primarias se eliminan de "
"primer orden respecto a la profundidad (o el tiempo) en el filtro de "
"flóculos. Con estos dos modelos, es posible por primera vez optimizar el "
"diseño de un floculador minimizando el volumen del floculador y filtro de "
"flóculos reactores."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:85
msgid "From the floc model we have"
msgstr "Del modelo de floc tenemos"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:87
msgid ""
"       "
"\\frac{dC_{P}}{dt}=-\\pi\\bar{\\alpha}kC_{P}\\left(\\frac{6}{\\pi}\\frac{C_{P}}{\\rho_P}\\right)^{2/3}"
" \\tilde{G}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:93
msgid ""
"From the floc filter we know that particle removal is first order with "
"respect to depth of the floc filter or time in the floc filter. We can use "
"floc filter data to estimate the first order rate constant."
msgstr ""
"Por el filtro de flóculos sabemos que la eliminación de partículas es de "
"primer orden respecto a la profundidad del filtro de flóculos o tiempo en el"
" filtro de flóculos. Podemos usar filtro de flóculos datos para estimar la "
"constante de tasa de primer orden."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:95
msgid "       \\frac{dC_{P}}{dt}=-k_{ff}C_{P}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:100
msgid "Separate variables to integrate this rate equation."
msgstr "Variables separadas para integrar esta ecuación de tasa."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:102
msgid "       \\frac{dC_{P}}{C_{P}}=-k_{ff}dt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:107
msgid "We integrate this to solve for the rate constant."
msgstr "Integramos esto para resolver la constante de tasa."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:109
msgid "       k_{ff} = -\\frac{1}{\\theta_{ff}}ln{\\frac{C_{P}}{C_{P_0}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:114
msgid ""
"We will use the previous equation to estimate the rate constant for the floc"
" filter."
msgstr ""
"Usaremos la ecuación anterior para estimar la constante de tasa para la "
"filtro de flóculos."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:116
msgid ""
"We can obtain a minimum volume design by setting the rate of primary "
"particle loss at the end of the flocculator to be equal to the rate of "
"primary particle loss at the beginning of the floc filter."
msgstr ""
"Podemos obtener un diseño de volumen mínimo estableciendo la tasa de pérdida"
" de partículas primarias al final del floculador igual a la tasa de pérdida "
"de partículas primarias al inicio del filtro de flóculos."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:118
msgid ""
"       "
"-k_{ff}C_{P}=-\\pi\\bar{\\alpha}kC_{P}\\left(\\frac{6}{\\pi}\\frac{C_{P}}{\\rho_P}\\right)^{2/3}"
" \\tilde{G}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:123
msgid ""
"Now we solve the previous equation for the target concentration of primary "
"particles that we should design for at the end of the flocculator."
msgstr ""
"Ahora resolvemos la ecuación anterior para la concentración objetivo de "
"partículas primarias que deberíamos diseñar al final del floculador."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:125
msgid ""
"      C_{P_{floc out}} = \\frac{\\pi \\rho_P}{6} \\left( "
"\\frac{k_{ff}}{\\pi\\bar{\\alpha}k \\tilde{G}}\\right)^{3/2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:131
msgid ""
"The concentration of primary particles at the flocculator effluent will be a"
" function of the flocculator velocity gradient."
msgstr ""
"La concentración de partículas primarias en el efluente del floculador será "
"función del gradiente de velocidad del floculador."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:133
msgid ""
"The next step is to determine the Gt for the flocculator given this effluent"
" flocculator particle concentration. The approximate equation for"
msgstr ""
"El siguiente paso es determinar el Gt para el floculador dada la "
"concentración de partículas floculadoras de este efluente. La ecuación "
"aproximada para"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:135
msgid ""
" \\tilde{G}\\theta \\approx \\frac{3}{2} \\frac{\\Lambda^2}{k \\pi D_P^2 "
"\\alpha}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:141
msgid "where the particle separation distance is given by"
msgstr "donde la distancia de separación de partículas viene dada por"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:143
msgid ""
"\\Lambda = \\left( \\frac{\\pi D_P^3}{6} \\frac{\\rho_P}{C_P} "
"\\right)^\\frac{1}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:148
msgid "Putting the previous two equations together we have:"
msgstr "Juntando las dos ecuaciones anteriores obtenemos:"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:150
msgid ""
" \\tilde{G}\\theta \\approx \\frac{3}{2} \\frac{1}{k \\pi D_P^2 \\alpha} "
"\\left( \\frac{\\pi D_P^3}{6} \\frac{\\rho_P}{C_P} \\right)^\\frac{2}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:155
msgid "We can simplify this equation because the particle size cancels out."
msgstr "Podemos simplificar esta ecuación porque el tamaño de la partícula se anula."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:157
msgid ""
" \\tilde{G}\\theta \\approx \\frac{3}{2} \\frac{1}{k \\pi \\alpha} \\left( "
"\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\frac{\\rho_P}{C_P} \\right)^\\frac{2}{3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:163
msgid ""
"Now we can substitute the equation for the optimal flocculated water primary"
" particle concentrations into the flocculator performance equation."
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos sustituir la ecuación de las concentraciones óptimas de "
"partículas primarias de agua floculada en la ecuación de rendimiento del "
"floculador."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:165
msgid ""
" \\tilde{G}\\theta \\approx \\frac{3}{2} \\frac{1}{k \\pi \\alpha} \\left( "
"\\frac{\\pi\\bar{\\alpha}k \\tilde{G}}{k_{ff}}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:170
msgid ""
"This simplifies to a very simple relationship that gives the optimal "
"flocculator residence time. This analysis assumes that the cost per volume "
"of flocculator is the same as the cost per volume of floc filter."
msgstr ""
"Esto se simplifica a una relación muy simple que proporciona el tiempo "
"óptimo de residencia del floculador. Este análisis asume que el coste por "
"volumen del floculador es el mismo que el coste por volumen de filtro de "
"flóculos."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:172
msgid "\\theta \\approx \\frac{3}{2} \\left( \\frac{1}{k_{ff}}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:177
msgid ""
"We now have an equation for the optimal flocculator residence time! It is a "
"function of the floc filter rate constant. The analysis below suggests that "
"the optimal flocculator residence time is about 300 seconds (5 minutes). "
"This analysis does not provide guidance on the optimal amount of energy to "
"be used in that flocculator. Overall plant performance is a function of how "
"much energy is used in flocculation and so that would need to be an economic"
" analysis. Startup performance when the floc filter is not yet formed is a "
"function of the energy dissipation rate."
msgstr ""
"¡Ahora tenemos una ecuación para el tiempo óptimo de residencia del "
"floculador! Es función de la constante de tasa de filtro de flóculos . El "
"análisis a continuación sugiere que el tiempo óptimo de residencia del "
"floculador es de unos 300 segundos (5 minutos). Este análisis no proporciona"
" orientación sobre la cantidad óptima de energía que se debe utilizar en ese"
" floculador. El rendimiento general de la planta depende de cuánta energía "
"se utilice en la floculación, por lo que eso debería ser un análisis "
"económico. El rendimiento de arranque cuando el filtro de flóculos aún no se"
" ha formado depende de la tasa de disipación de energía."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Theory_and_Future_Work.rst:179
msgid ""
"This analysis suggests that a residence time that is less than what we are "
"currently using for civil works AguaClara plants (about 8 minutes) and "
"greater than what we are using for the PF300 (1-2 minutes) is the optimal "
"solution. High velocity gradients for flocculators with this long of a "
"residence time will require a lot of head loss. We need to make sure that we"
" are using a reasonable amount of energy."
msgstr ""
"Este análisis sugiere que un tiempo de residencia menor que el que usamos "
"actualmente para las plantas de obras civiles de AguaClara (unos 8 minutos) "
"y mayor que el que usamos para el PF300 (1-2 minutos) es la solución óptima."
" Gradientes de velocidad elevados para floculadores con un tiempo de "
"residencia tan largo requerirán mucha pérdida de carga. Debemos asegurarnos "
"de que estamos usando una cantidad razonable de energía."

